tters against them that are quiet in the land.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)And said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen it.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter#«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.This thou hast seen, O LORD: keep not silence:¦layout ‚¤text»O Lord, be not far from me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'Even unto my cause, my God and my Lord.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ8Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness;¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And let them not rejoice over me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter#«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ:Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it:¦layout ‚¤textÙ+Let them not say, We have swallowed him up.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙPLet them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at mine hurt:¦layout ‚¤textÙPLet them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify themselves against me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter#«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙDLet them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause:¦layout ‚¤textÙoYea, let them say continually, Let the LORD be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And of thy praise all the day long.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse